1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,654
Ava: What if an attention kernel gets much faster, but the training step barely moves?
Ava：如果注意力内核快了很多，单步训练却几乎没变快，会怎样？

2
00:00:05,654 --> 00:00:08,726
That's the puzzle in this PyTorch post.
这就是这篇 PyTorch 文章探讨的问题。

3
00:00:08,726 --> 00:00:09,393
Brian: Exactly.
Brian：没错。

4
00:00:09,393 --> 00:00:18,142
The team extended FlashAttention-4, or FA4, to use MXFP8, a microscaling eight-bit floating-point format.
团队扩展了 FlashAttention-4（FA4），使其支持 MXFP8，一种微缩放 8 位浮点格式。

5
00:00:18,142 --> 00:00:25,324
Then they tackled the work around attention, where a kernel speedup can disappear.
随后，他们着手优化注意力计算的周边环节，因为内核提速可能在这些环节被抵消。

6
00:00:25,324 --> 00:00:31,890
Ava: So the headline isn't just, “Blackwell can multiply smaller numbers faster”?
Ava：所以重点不只是“Blackwell 能更快地乘小数字”？

7
00:00:31,890 --> 00:00:36,836
Brian: Right. Blackwell's tensor cores have block-scaled MMA instructions.
Brian：对。Blackwell 的张量核心支持块缩放 MMA 指令。

8
00:00:36,836 --> 00:00:39,863
MMA means matrix multiply-and-accumulate.
MMA 指矩阵乘加。

9
00:00:39,863 --> 00:00:50,696
The post says these instructions offer two to four times the throughput of BF16, or bfloat sixteen, MMA, depending on the microscaling format.
文章称，根据微缩放格式的不同，这些指令的吞吐量是 BF16（16 位脑浮点）MMA 的 2 到 4 倍。

10
00:00:50,696 --> 00:00:55,150
Ava: But that's hardware throughput. What gets in the way during training?
Ava：但那是硬件吞吐量。训练时有什么阻碍？

11
00:00:55,150 --> 00:01:00,598
Brian: You have to quantize values into the smaller format and manage scale factors.
Brian：得把数值量化成更小的格式，还要管理缩放因子。

12
00:01:00,598 --> 00:01:04,773
Those scales tell the hardware how to interpret each block.
这些缩放因子告诉硬件如何解读每个数据块。

13
00:01:04,773 --> 00:01:10,500
Moving values and scales can cost enough to erase the faster multiplication.
搬运数值和缩放因子的开销，可能足以抵消乘法的提速。

14
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:16,274
Ava: Like buying a faster oven, then spending dinner time measuring every ingredient?
Ava：就像买了更快的烤箱，做饭的时间却都花在称量食材上？

15
00:01:16,274 --> 00:01:22,953
Brian: Pretty much. Attention adds another problem: some values are created inside the kernel.
Brian：差不多。注意力计算还有个难题：有些数值是在内核里生成的。

16
00:01:22,953 --> 00:01:27,448
You can't prepare every quantized input ahead of time.
没法提前量化所有输入。

17
00:01:27,448 --> 00:01:31,854
Ava: Let's start with the forward pass. What actually happens there?
Ava：先说前向传播。这里具体发生了什么？

18
00:01:31,854 --> 00:01:35,524
Brian: Queries and keys produce attention scores.
Brian：查询向量和键向量计算出注意力分数。

19
00:01:35,524 --> 00:01:44,260
Softmax turns those scores into weights, called P. Then P combines the values to produce the output.
Softmax 将这些分数转换为称作 P 的权重。随后 P 对各个值加权求和，得到输出。

20
00:01:44,260 --> 00:01:49,940
The post calls the inputs Q, K, and V: query, key, and value.
文章把输入称为 Q、K 和 V，分别是查询、键和值。

21
00:01:49,940 --> 00:01:55,810
Ava: And P only exists after softmax. Is that one of the awkward inputs?
Ava：而 P 要经过 softmax 才会产生。它也是难处理的输入之一吗？

22
00:01:55,810 --> 00:02:02,002
Brian: Yes. Softmax computes P in FP32, meaning thirty-two-bit floating point.
Brian：是。Softmax 用 FP32，也就是 32 位浮点数，计算 P。

23
00:02:02,002 --> 00:02:14,736
Earlier, P was converted to BF16 before the multiplication with V. This version converts P to MXFP8 and computes its scales inside the kernel.
此前，P 在与 V 相乘前会转换为 BF16。这个版本在核函数内部将 P 转换为 MXFP8，并计算其缩放系数。

24
00:02:14,736 --> 00:02:20,126
Ava: Wait, do all those scales follow the same direction through the tensor?
Ava：等等，这些缩放因子在张量中都是沿同一个方向排列的吗？

25
00:02:20,126 --> 00:02:26,720
Brian: They don't. Block-scaled MMA needs scales along the dimension being multiplied over.
Brian：不是。块缩放 MMA 要求缩放因子沿着乘法的归约维度排列。

26
00:02:26,720 --> 00:02:30,174
For Q and K, that's the embedding dimension.
对 Q 和 K 来说，这个维度是嵌入维度。

27
00:02:30,174 --> 00:02:35,548
For V in the multiplication with P, it's the sequence dimension.
对与 P 相乘的 V 来说，则是序列维度。

28
00:02:35,548 --> 00:02:39,666
Ava: So even the layout of the scale factors matters.
Ava：所以缩放因子的布局也很重要。

29
00:02:39,666 --> 00:02:40,158
Brian: A lot.
Brian：非常重要。

30
00:02:40,158 --> 00:02:49,102
The kernel loads them through TMA, the tile-loading mechanism described in the post, and places them in TMEM.
内核通过文章介绍的分块加载机制 TMA 加载它们，再放入 TMEM。

31
00:02:49,102 --> 00:02:54,704
TMEM is tensor memory used for operands and accumulated results.
TMEM 是存放操作数和累加结果的张量内存。

32
00:02:54,704 --> 00:03:00,022
Ava: Is there room for them? I remember the post saying TMEM was already full.
Ava：还有地方放吗？我记得文章说 TMEM 已经满了。

33
00:03:00,022 --> 00:03:02,800
Brian: That's the central forward-pass puzzle.
Brian：这正是前向传播的核心难题。

34
00:03:02,800 --> 00:03:09,494
Blackwell has five hundred and twelve TMEM columns, and the existing FA4 layout uses them all.
Blackwell 有 512 列 TMEM，现有的 FA4 布局已经全部占满。

35
00:03:09,494 --> 00:03:15,684
The team puts scales in regions whose earlier contents have already been consumed.
团队把缩放因子放进原有数据已被用完的区域。

36
00:03:15,684 --> 00:03:20,642
Ava: That sounds like reusing a desk as soon as someone finishes their paperwork.
Ava：就像一个人处理完文件，马上把桌子腾给下一个人。

37
00:03:20,642 --> 00:03:25,506
Brian: Yes, with careful timing. FA4 alternates between two query tiles.
Brian：对，但时机得把握好。FA4 会在两个查询数据块之间交替处理。

38
00:03:25,506 --> 00:03:32,167
Some scales go where an output hasn't started yet; others go where a score has been read.
有些缩放因子放在尚未开始写入输出的区域，另一些放在分数已被读取的区域。

39
00:03:32,167 --> 00:03:38,728
One reuse needs an extra barrier to prevent two asynchronous writes from colliding.
其中一次复用需要额外的屏障，防止两次异步写入相互冲突。

40
00:03:38,728 --> 00:03:42,102
Ava: Does that barrier slow everything down?
Ava：这个屏障会拖慢整体速度吗？

41
00:03:42,102 --> 00:03:45,176
Brian: The authors say it usually doesn't add cost.
Brian：作者说，它通常不会增加开销。

42
00:03:45,176 --> 00:03:51,744
Another matrix multiplication typically overlaps the read that must happen before the barrier.
因为必须在屏障前完成的读取，通常会与另一次矩阵乘法重叠执行。

43
00:03:51,744 --> 00:03:57,404
That's a scheduling claim about their kernel, rather than a general promise.
这是针对他们内核调度方式的说法，并非普遍保证。

44
00:03:57,404 --> 00:04:04,786
Ava: Okay. Faster multiplication also changes which part of the pipeline feels slow, right?
Ava：好。乘法变快后，流水线中显得慢的环节也会变，对吧？

45
00:04:04,786 --> 00:04:10,253
Brian: Right. Softmax takes about the same kind of work while MMA gets faster.
Brian：对。Softmax 的工作量基本不变，MMA 却变快了。

46
00:04:10,253 --> 00:04:14,950
Delays once hidden behind BF16 multiplication become visible.
以前被 BF16 乘法掩盖的延迟，现在显现出来了。

47
00:04:14,950 --> 00:04:21,768
At tile boundaries, the next softmax can wait for the next query-key multiplication.
在数据块交界处，下一次 softmax 可能要等下一次查询与键的矩阵乘法。

48
00:04:21,768 --> 00:04:24,854
Ava: How do they give softmax a head start?
Ava：他们怎么让 softmax 提前开始？

49
00:04:24,854 --> 00:04:29,843
Brian: With unroll-KV, a schedule that interleaves work on key and value tiles.
Brian：采用 unroll-KV，让键和值分块的计算交错进行。

50
00:04:29,843 --> 00:04:39,964
They move the first query-key multiplication for the next tile earlier, alongside the final multiplication with values from the current tile.
他们提前执行下一个分块中查询与键的首次乘法，同时完成当前分块与值的最后一次乘法。

51
00:04:39,964 --> 00:04:43,098
Ava: Nice. Was it a free win?
Ava：不错。这是白捡的性能提升吗？

52
00:04:43,098 --> 00:04:49,097
Brian: No. That change initially slowed the BF16 path because it delayed correction work.
Brian：不是。起初，这项改动拖慢了 BF16 路径，因为它推迟了校正计算。

53
00:04:49,097 --> 00:04:55,315
They moved a barrier wait until after a row-sum calculation that didn't depend on it.
他们把屏障等待移到不依赖它的行求和计算之后。

54
00:04:55,315 --> 00:04:58,664
That kept the correction pipeline moving.
这样校正流水线就能持续运行。

55
00:04:58,664 --> 00:05:05,182
Ava: And the online conversion of P? Computing a scale for every block sounds expensive.
Ava：那 P 的在线转换呢？每个分块都计算缩放因子，听起来很费时。

56
00:05:05,182 --> 00:05:06,040
Brian: It could be.
Brian：确实可能如此。

57
00:05:06,040 --> 00:05:12,762
The post describes short instruction sequences for finding block maxima and converting values.
文章介绍了用简短的指令序列寻找分块最大值并转换数值。

58
00:05:12,762 --> 00:05:23,124
It also reuses a maximum from softmax, avoiding extra maximum calculations while adding one exponential calculation per thirty-two elements.
它还复用 softmax 的最大值，省去额外的最大值计算，代价是每 32 个元素多算一次指数函数。

59
00:05:23,124 --> 00:05:31,250
Ava: Let me recap: they find space for scales, keep softmax busy, and quantize P as it's produced.
Ava：我总结一下：他们为缩放因子腾出空间，让 softmax 持续运转，并在生成 P 时将其量化。

60
00:05:31,250 --> 00:05:33,001
Brian: That's the forward kernel.
Brian：这说的是前向计算核。

61
00:05:33,001 --> 00:05:41,704
Now backward brings a different headache: the same tensor may feed matrix multiplications that read it along different axes.
反向计算有另一个难题：同一个张量可能用于沿不同轴读取它的矩阵乘法。

62
00:05:41,704 --> 00:05:46,110
Ava: Why can't they just transpose the already quantized data?
Ava：为什么不能直接转置已量化的数据？

63
00:05:46,110 --> 00:05:51,389
Brian: Ordinary block scaling groups values along the multiplication dimension.
Brian：常规分块缩放沿乘法维度对数值分组。

64
00:05:51,389 --> 00:05:54,542
After a transpose, those groups can change.
转置后，这些分组可能改变。

65
00:05:54,542 --> 00:05:59,732
Separate quantized copies would mean extra conversion and storage.
分别保存量化副本会增加转换和存储开销。

66
00:05:59,732 --> 00:06:02,794
Ava: So what's their way around that?
Ava：那他们怎么解决？

67
00:06:02,794 --> 00:06:09,231
Brian: They quantize Q, K, and the output gradient using thirty-two by thirty-two square blocks.
Brian：他们以 32×32 的方形分块量化 Q、K 和输出梯度。

68
00:06:09,231 --> 00:06:19,344
A square block stays the same block after transposition, so both multiplication directions can share one quantized data representation.
方形分块转置后仍是同一分块，因此两个乘法方向可以共用一份量化数据。

69
00:06:19,344 --> 00:06:23,534
Ava: The payload is shared. Are the scales shared too?
Ava：数据共用了。缩放因子也共用吗？

70
00:06:23,534 --> 00:06:31,209
Brian: Their values can be reused, but the smaller scale tensors still need layouts suited to each tensor-core multiplication.
Brian：数值可以复用，但较小的缩放因子张量仍需采用适合各次张量核心乘法的布局。

71
00:06:31,209 --> 00:06:37,492
Think of keeping the same books while arranging their index cards for two different readers.
就像保留同一批书，却为两位读者分别整理索引卡。

72
00:06:37,492 --> 00:06:41,723
Ava: And what about dS, the gradient of the attention scores?
Ava：那注意力分数的梯度 dS 呢？

73
00:06:41,723 --> 00:06:44,490
That's computed during backward.
它是在反向计算中得到的。

74
00:06:44,490 --> 00:06:49,798
Brian: They quantize each thirty-two by thirty-two block of dS once as well.
Brian：他们也只量化每个 32×32 的 dS 分块一次。

75
00:06:49,798 --> 00:06:56,030
A warp, meaning a group of GPU threads, finds the block's largest absolute value.
一个 warp，也就是一组 GPU 线程，找出分块中的最大绝对值。

76
00:06:56,030 --> 00:07:01,688
The square block then works for both multiplications that consume dS.
这个方形分块随后可供两次使用 dS 的乘法共用。

77
00:07:01,688 --> 00:07:05,446
Ava: Does backward have the same TMEM space problem?
Ava：反向计算也有 TMEM 空间问题吗？

78
00:07:05,446 --> 00:07:09,717
Brian: Yes, with five matrix multiplications competing for space.
Brian：有，五次矩阵乘法都要争用空间。

79
00:07:09,717 --> 00:07:14,062
Two gradient accumulators stay in TMEM throughout the loop.
两个梯度累加器在整个循环中都留在 TMEM 里。

80
00:07:14,062 --> 00:07:24,060
The team reuses the remaining regions for scales and reports needing one additional barrier on the one-CTA path they use for MXFP8.
团队把剩余区域复用于缩放因子，并报告称，MXFP8 所用的单 CTA 路径需要额外一个屏障。

81
00:07:24,060 --> 00:07:29,162
Ava: There's also a dQ reduction change. Why did that matter?
Ava：dQ 归约也有改动。为什么这很重要？

82
00:07:29,162 --> 00:07:30,922
Brian: dQ is the query gradient.
Brian：dQ 是查询的梯度。

83
00:07:30,922 --> 00:07:38,878
The kernel writes a tile of it to global memory on every inner-loop iteration, so bandwidth becomes a bottleneck.
计算核在内层循环的每次迭代都会把一个分块写入全局内存，因此带宽成了瓶颈。

84
00:07:38,878 --> 00:07:46,480
In their workloads, FP16, or sixteen-bit floating point, with static scaling gave the best performance.
在他们的工作负载中，采用静态缩放的 FP16（16 位浮点数）性能最好。

85
00:07:46,480 --> 00:07:50,118
Ava: That accuracy choice sounds workload dependent.
Ava：这种精度选择似乎取决于工作负载。

86
00:07:50,118 --> 00:07:52,034
Brian: It is presented that way.
Brian：作者也是这么表述的。

87
00:07:52,034 --> 00:08:01,306
The authors say their dQ values remain small and this approach has acceptable numerical accuracy in production workloads.
作者称，他们的 dQ 数值始终较小，这种方法在生产工作负载中有可接受的数值精度。

88
00:08:01,306 --> 00:08:05,564
They also report results with FP32 dQ accumulation.
他们也报告了使用 FP32 累加 dQ 的结果。

89
00:08:05,564 --> 00:08:07,575
Ava: We've sped up attention itself.
Ava：注意力计算本身已经加速了。

90
00:08:07,575 --> 00:08:12,466
How do they stop quantization outside the kernel from eating the gain?
怎样避免计算核之外的量化耗掉这些收益？

91
00:08:12,466 --> 00:08:16,072
Brian: They fuse quantization into producer kernels.
Brian：他们把量化融合进上游计算核。

92
00:08:16,072 --> 00:08:21,521
RMSNorm, or root mean square normalization, can emit MXFP8 directly.
RMSNorm，也就是均方根归一化，可以直接输出 MXFP8。

93
00:08:21,521 --> 00:08:32,688
Projection GEMMs, meaning general matrix multiplications, can convert their results to MXFP8 in the epilogue, their final output stage.
投影 GEMM，也就是通用矩阵乘法，可以在收尾输出阶段把结果转换为 MXFP8。

94
00:08:32,688 --> 00:08:37,214
Ava: So the intermediate doesn't make a round trip through global memory?
Ava：这样中间结果就不用在全局内存里来回读写了？

95
00:08:37,214 --> 00:08:37,843
Brian: Exactly.
Brian：没错。

96
00:08:37,843 --> 00:08:44,681
The GEMM result moves from TMEM to registers, gets converted there, and is written out.
GEMM 的结果从 TMEM 移到寄存器，在那里转换后写出。

97
00:08:44,681 --> 00:08:48,612
The BF16 intermediate never reaches global memory.
BF16 中间结果完全不会进入全局内存。

98
00:08:48,612 --> 00:08:57,844
Their fused RMSNorm kernel also waits until it has seen all thirty-two rows needed for each square block's scale.
他们融合后的 RMSNorm 计算核也会等到收齐每个方形分块计算缩放因子所需的全部 32 行。

99
00:08:57,844 --> 00:09:02,850
Ava: The post talks about jagged sequences too. What's jagged here?
Ava：文章还谈到变长序列。这里的“变长”是什么意思？

100
00:09:02,850 --> 00:09:05,836
Brian: Different sequences have different lengths.
Brian：不同序列的长度不同。

101
00:09:05,836 --> 00:09:12,571
Their natural offsets often don't meet the alignment required by Blackwell's scale-factor layout.
它们原本的偏移位置往往不符合 Blackwell 缩放因子布局的对齐要求。

102
00:09:12,571 --> 00:09:17,504
Padding every FP8 activation would add storage and memory traffic.
如果给所有 FP8 激活值补齐，会增加存储占用和内存传输量。

103
00:09:17,504 --> 00:09:19,942
Ava: What gets padded instead?
Ava：那补齐的是什么？

104
00:09:19,942 --> 00:09:22,604
Brian: Only the much smaller scale factors.
Brian：只补齐小得多的缩放因子。

105
00:09:22,604 --> 00:09:26,523
The FP8 data stays compact at its original positions.
FP8 数据仍紧凑地保留在原来的位置。

106
00:09:26,523 --> 00:09:34,860
When a consumer loads tiles, it uses padded addresses for scales and the original jagged addresses for data.
后续算子加载数据块时，用补齐后的地址读取缩放因子，用原来的变长地址读取数据。

107
00:09:34,860 --> 00:09:40,562
Ava: That's the zero-gather idea: move the little labels, leave the big boxes alone?
Ava：这就是 zero-gather 的思路：挪动小标签，大箱子不动？

108
00:09:40,562 --> 00:09:42,027
Brian: That's a good picture.
Brian：这个比喻很贴切。

109
00:09:42,027 --> 00:09:48,222
Lightweight kernels rearrange scale-factor bytes into the layouts the next operation expects.
轻量级内核会重新排列缩放因子的字节，使其符合下一步运算需要的布局。

110
00:09:48,222 --> 00:09:57,232
The team also extends a downstream weight-gradient GEMM to handle each variable-length sequence as its own multiplication segment.
团队还扩展了后续的权重梯度 GEMM，让每条变长序列分别作为一个矩阵乘法片段处理。

111
00:09:57,232 --> 00:10:02,118
Ava: Let's get to the measurements. Where do the big kernel numbers come from?
Ava：来说说测试数据。这些亮眼的内核数据来自哪里？

112
00:10:02,118 --> 00:10:07,668
Brian: From benchmarks on Meta's internal recommendation-system GB300 GPUs.
Brian：来自 Meta 内部推荐系统所用 GB300 GPU 的基准测试。

113
00:10:07,668 --> 00:10:21,404
On large language model shapes, their MXFP8 FA4 forward kernel reaches two point eight five petaflops per second, versus two point zero for their internal BF16 FA4.
在大语言模型的张量形状下，他们的 MXFP8 FA4 前向内核达到 2.85 PFLOPS，而内部 BF16 FA4 为 2.0 PFLOPS。

114
00:10:21,404 --> 00:10:27,226
Ava: That's about one point four three times faster. What happens in backward?
Ava：大约快了 1.43 倍。反向计算呢？

115
00:10:27,226 --> 00:10:38,558
Brian: On those shapes, it reaches one point eight two petaflops per second with FP32 dQ accumulation, or one point nine eight with FP16 dQ.
Brian：在这些形状下，使用 FP32 dQ 累加时达到 1.82 PFLOPS，使用 FP16 dQ 时达到 1.98 PFLOPS。

116
00:10:38,558 --> 00:10:42,912
The BF16 cuDNN baseline is one point five zero.
BF16 cuDNN 基线为 1.50 PFLOPS。

117
00:10:42,912 --> 00:10:49,238
Ava: Their internal recommendation shapes are different from the large language model shapes, aren't they?
Ava：他们内部推荐系统的张量形状与大语言模型不同，对吧？

118
00:10:49,238 --> 00:10:56,892
Brian: Yes: higher batch size, fewer heads, shorter queries, and highly jagged sequence lengths.
Brian：对，批量更大、头数更少、查询更短，而且序列长度很不规则。

119
00:10:56,892 --> 00:11:09,196
On a reported jagged forward case, MXFP8 reaches two point five four petaflops per second, versus one point six zero for internal BF16 FA4.
在报告的一组变长序列前向测试中，MXFP8 达到 2.54 PFLOPS，内部 BF16 FA4 为 1.60 PFLOPS。

120
00:11:09,196 --> 00:11:11,754
Ava: And the internal backward result?
Ava：内部场景的反向计算结果呢？

121
00:11:11,754 --> 00:11:23,476
Brian: One point five eight petaflops per second with FP16 dQ accumulation, a one point five two times gain over their internal BF16 FA4.
Brian：使用 FP16 dQ 累加时为 1.58 PFLOPS，比内部 BF16 FA4 快 1.52 倍。

122
00:11:23,476 --> 00:11:28,424
With FP32 dQ accumulation, it's one point four two.
使用 FP32 dQ 累加时为 1.42 PFLOPS。

123
00:11:28,424 --> 00:11:32,686
Ava: Do those impressive kernel gains survive in the whole module?
Ava：这些亮眼的内核提速，在整个模块上也能体现吗？

124
00:11:32,686 --> 00:11:33,245
Brian: Some do.
Brian：有一部分能。

125
00:11:33,245 --> 00:11:41,067
On their single-GPU module test, four thousand and ninety-six key-value tokens show essentially no latency gain.
在单 GPU 模块测试中，键值令牌数为 4096 时，延迟基本没有改善。

126
00:11:41,067 --> 00:11:47,772
At eight thousand one hundred and ninety-two tokens, it's one point one eight times faster.
达到 8192 个令牌时，速度提升至 1.18 倍。

127
00:11:47,772 --> 00:11:50,930
Ava: And at the longest tested length?
Ava：测试的最长长度呢？

128
00:11:50,930 --> 00:12:02,577
Brian: At sixteen thousand three hundred and eighty-four tokens, median forward-plus-backward latency falls from about thirty-one point seven milliseconds to twenty-four point five.
Brian：达到 16384 个令牌时，前向加反向计算的延迟中位数从约 31.7 毫秒降至 24.5 毫秒。

129
00:12:02,577 --> 00:12:05,872
That's a one point three zero times speedup.
相当于快了 1.30 倍。

130
00:12:05,872 --> 00:12:09,894
Ava: That smallest case is a useful reality check.
Ava：最短长度的结果很能提醒我们看清实际效果。

131
00:12:09,894 --> 00:12:10,307
Brian: It is.
Brian：是的。

132
00:12:10,307 --> 00:12:17,608
The post says these recommendation shapes can be bandwidth bound, so conversion and memory traffic matter.
文章说，这类推荐系统的张量形状可能受内存带宽限制，因此格式转换和内存传输量很关键。

133
00:12:17,608 --> 00:12:23,468
Fusing the producers and keeping jagged data compact help the end-to-end result.
融合上游算子、保持变长数据紧凑，有助于提升端到端表现。

134
00:12:23,468 --> 00:12:27,562
Ava: How do they check what the lower precision does to the answers?
Ava：他们怎么检查低精度对结果的影响？

135
00:12:27,562 --> 00:12:33,879
Brian: They report SQNR, signal-to-quantization-noise ratio, against a BF16 reference.
Brian：他们以 BF16 结果为参考，报告了 SQNR，也就是信号与量化噪声比。

136
00:12:33,879 --> 00:12:37,638
Higher means less error relative to the signal.
数值越高，误差相对于信号就越小。

137
00:12:37,638 --> 00:12:46,224
They also say MXFP8 attention had a neutral training outcome while productionizing this module for GEM.
他们还说，在为 GEM 推进该模块的生产应用时，MXFP8 注意力计算对训练结果没有明显影响。

138
00:12:46,224 --> 00:12:49,310
Ava: Any comparison we should handle carefully?
Ava：有没有哪项对比需要谨慎看待？

139
00:12:49,310 --> 00:12:49,626
Brian: Yes.
Brian：有。

140
00:12:49,626 --> 00:12:58,638
In their tests, cuDNN MXFP8 backward disagreed with the reference for two gradients when V scales were nonuniform.
在他们的测试中，当 V 的缩放因子不一致时，cuDNN MXFP8 的反向计算有两项梯度与参考结果不符。

141
00:12:58,638 --> 00:13:06,701
They treat its reported backward throughput as performance-only, not an accuracy-qualified comparison.
因此，他们报告的反向吞吐量只能用于性能对比，不能视为通过精度验证的对比。

142
00:13:06,701 --> 00:13:10,924
That caveat doesn't apply to cuDNN MXFP8 forward.
这一限制不适用于 cuDNN MXFP8 的前向计算。

143
00:13:10,924 --> 00:13:18,666
Ava: And their square-block quantization and FP16 dQ choices were checked on their training workloads?
Ava：方形块量化和 FP16 dQ 这些选择，也在他们的训练任务上验证过？

144
00:13:18,666 --> 00:13:23,889
Brian: Right. The article says those choices were numerically acceptable there.
Brian：对。文章说，在那些任务上，这些选择的数值表现可以接受。

145
00:13:23,889 --> 00:13:28,736
It doesn't establish the same result for every model or shape.
但这不代表所有模型或张量形状都能得到同样的结果。

146
00:13:28,736 --> 00:13:32,158
Ava: Give me the three-point recap before we go.
Ava：结束前，帮我用三点回顾一下。

147
00:13:32,158 --> 00:13:37,918
Brian: First, faster block-scaled MMA needs careful TMEM placement and scheduling.
Brian：第一，更快的块缩放 MMA 需要仔细安排 TMEM 中的数据位置和执行时序。

148
00:13:37,918 --> 00:13:43,832
Second, square-block quantization lets backward reuse data across transposes.
第二，方形块量化让反向计算能在转置前后复用数据。

149
00:13:43,832 --> 00:13:51,324
Third, fused producers and compact jagged data carry more of the kernel gain into the module.
第三，融合的上游算子和紧凑的变长数据，让更多内核性能提升体现在整个模块上。

150
00:13:51,324 --> 00:14:00,314
Ava: And the payoff depends on the workload: the longest tested module case gains most, while the shortest barely changes.
Ava：效果取决于负载：测试中最长的模块用例提升最大，最短的几乎没有变化。

151
00:14:00,314 --> 00:14:06,904
Brian: Exactly. That's our look at low precision FA4. See you next time.
Brian：没错。以上就是我们对低精度 FA4 的介绍。下次见。
